<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28989" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mēvānĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in Umbria</i>, now <i>Bevagna</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 9, 41, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 3, 8,
			3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 6, 647</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nebulosa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 1, 123.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mēvānas</span></b> ,
				ātis, <i>comm., of</i> or
				<i>belonging to the city of Mevania</i> Mevanas
			Varenus, <i><span class="en">Sil. 4, 546</span></i>.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mēvānā-tes</span></b> ,
				ĭum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Mevania, Mevanians</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 14,
				19, § 113</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mē-vānĭensis</span></b> ,
			e, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Mevania, Mevanian</i>: boves, Philar. ad <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 2,
				146</span></i>.</div>
